## Usage Example

```tsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import PrimaryButton from './PrimaryButton';

export default function Demo() {
  const [saving, setSaving] = useState(false);

  const handleSave = async () => {
    setSaving(true);
    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 2000));
    setSaving(false);
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: '1rem', flexWrap: 'wrap' }}>
      <PrimaryButton onClick={() => alert('Clicked!')}>
        Default
      </PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton size="sm">Small</PrimaryButton>
      <PrimaryButton size="lg">Large</PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton disabled>Disabled</PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton loading={saving} onClick={handleSave}>
        Save Changes
      </PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton rightIcon={<span>→</span>}>
        Continue
      </PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton type="submit" fullWidth>
        Submit Form
      </PrimaryButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Key Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Hover** | Darker background, subtle lift, and glow shadow |
| **Active** | Even darker shade, pressed-down effect |
| **Disabled** | Muted gray, `not-allowed` cursor, no hover effects |
| **Loading** | Spinner overlay, button width preserved, clicks blocked |
| **Focus** | Visible ring for keyboard users only (`:focus-visible`) |
| **Accessibility** | `aria-disabled`, `aria-busy`, reduced-motion support |
| **Flexibility** | Forwards refs, passes through all native button props |
| **Safe default** | `type="button"` prevents accidental form submissions |

**Theming tip:** Because colors are CSS custom properties, you can retheme the button by overriding them, e.g. `.myTheme { --btn-bg: #059669; --btn-bg-hover: #047857; }`.

