## Key Features

| Feature | Details |
|---|---|
| **Hover state** | Darker background, lifted shadow, and a subtle upward shift. Applied only when enabled (`:not(:disabled)`). |
| **Disabled state** | Muted gray colors, `not-allowed` cursor, and no hover or active effects. Clicks are blocked natively and in the handler. |
| **Active state** | Pressed feedback with a darker shade and reset elevation. |
| **Focus ring** | Uses `:focus-visible`, so the ring appears for keyboard users but not on mouse clicks. |
| **Loading state** | Spinner overlay that keeps the button width stable. The button is disabled while loading and sets `aria-busy`. |
| **Accessibility** | Native `<button>`, `aria-disabled`, `aria-busy`, and support for reduced-motion preferences. |
| **Flexibility** | `forwardRef` support, passes through all native button props, and offers three sizes, a full-width option, and icons. |
| **Theming** | CSS custom properties make it easy to override colors per theme. |

> **Tip:** `type` defaults to `"button"` to prevent accidental form submissions. Pass `type="submit"` explicitly when you need one.

