## Features

- **Portal rendering**: the modal is mounted on `document.body`, so it avoids z-index and `overflow: hidden` problems from parent elements.
- **Darkened backdrop**: a semi-transparent overlay covers the viewport and fades in.
- **Centered panel**: flexbox centers the panel, and it scrolls internally when content is taller than the screen.
- **Several ways to close**: Escape, a backdrop click, or the × button. The backdrop listens to `onMouseDown`, so dragging a text selection out of the panel won't close the modal by accident.
- **Accessibility**: uses `role="dialog"` and `aria-modal`, links the title with `aria-labelledby`, traps Tab focus inside the panel, and returns focus to the trigger on close.
- **Scroll lock**: the page behind the modal can't scroll while it's open.
- **Stable focus**: `onClose` is kept in a ref, so an inline arrow function from the parent won't re-run the effect and pull focus back to the panel on each re-render.
- **Reduced motion**: animations are turned off for users who set that preference.

The component uses a fixed `id="modal-title"`, which only works if one modal is open at a time. If you might stack modals, generate the id with React's `useId()` instead.

