## Features

| Feature | How it works |
|---|---|
| **Darkened backdrop** | A fixed, full-screen overlay with `rgba(0,0,0,0.6)` |
| **Centered panel** | Flexbox centering on the backdrop |
| **Portal rendering** | Renders into `document.body` so parent `overflow` or `z-index` styles can't clip it |
| **Escape to close** | A `keydown` listener runs while the modal is open |
| **Backdrop click to close** | Checks `e.target === e.currentTarget` so clicks inside the panel don't close it. Can be turned off with `closeOnBackdropClick={false}` |
| **Focus trap** | Tab and Shift+Tab cycle through the focusable elements inside the panel |
| **Focus restore** | Returns focus to the element that opened the modal |
| **Scroll lock** | Disables body scrolling while open |
| **Accessibility** | Uses `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, `aria-labelledby`, and a labeled close button |
| **Animations** | Fade and slide-up entrance, turned off for users who set `prefers-reduced-motion` |

The backdrop uses `onMouseDown` rather than `onClick`. With `onClick`, a user who presses the mouse inside the panel (for example, while selecting text) and releases it over the backdrop would close the modal by accident.

Below is an accessible, reusable React modal component. It renders through a portal, darkens the page behind it, centers the panel, and handles keyboard focus and scroll locking.

## Modal.jsx

```jsx
import { useEffect, useRef, useId } from "react";
import { createPortal } from "react-dom";
import "./Modal.css";

const FOCUSABLE_SELECTORS = [
  "a[href]",
  "button:not([disabled])",
  "textarea:not([disabled])",
  "input:not([disabled])",
  "select:not([disabled])",
  '[tabindex]:not([tabindex="-1"])',
].join(",");

export default function Modal({
  isOpen,
  onClose,
  title,
  children,
  closeOnBackdropClick = true,
}) {
  const panelRef = useRef(null);
  const previouslyFocused = useRef(null);
  const titleId = useId();

  // Close on Escape + trap focus inside the panel
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;

    const handleKeyDown = (e) => {
      if (e.key === "Escape") {
        e.stopPropagation();
        onClose();
        return;
      }

      if (e.key === "Tab" && panelRef.current) {
        const focusable = panelRef.current.querySelectorAll(FOCUSABLE_SELECTORS);
        if (focusable.length === 0) {
          e.preventDefault();
          return;
        }
        const first = focusable[0];
        const last = focusable[focusable.length - 1];

        if (e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === first) {
          e.preventDefault();
          last.focus();
        } else if (!e.shiftKey && document.activeElement === last) {
          e.preventDefault();
          first.focus();
        }
      }
    };

    document.addEventListener("keydown", handleKeyDown);
    return () => document.removeEventListener("keydown", handleKeyDown);
  }, [isOpen, onClose]);

  // Lock body scroll and manage focus
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;

    previouslyFocused.current = document.activeElement;
    const originalOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";

    // Move focus into the modal
    const firstFocusable = panelRef.current?.querySelector(FOCUSABLE_SELECTORS);
    (firstFocusable || panelRef.current)?.focus();

    return () => {
      document.body.style.overflow = originalOverflow;
      previouslyFocused.current?.focus?.(); // restore focus to the trigger
    };
  }, [isOpen]);

  if (!isOpen) return null;

  const handleBackdropMouseDown = (e) => {
    // Only close when the press starts on the backdrop itself
    if (closeOnBackdropClick && e.target === e.currentTarget) {
      onClose();
    }
  };

  return createPortal(
    <div className="modal-backdrop" onMouseDown={handleBackdropMouseDown}>
      <div
        ref={panelRef}
        className="modal-panel"
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby={title ? titleId : undefined}
        tabIndex={-1}
      >
        <div className="modal-header">
          {title && (
            <h2 id={titleId} className="modal-title">
              {title}
            </h2>
          )}
          <button
            type="button"
            className="modal-close"
            onClick={onClose}
            aria-label="Close modal"
          >
            &times;
          </button>
        </div>
        <div className="modal-body">{children}</div>
      </div>
    </div>,
    document.body
  );
}
```

