## Usage

```jsx
import { useState } from "react";
import Modal from "./Modal";

export default function App() {
  const [open, setOpen] = useState(false);

  return (
    <>
      <button onClick={() => setOpen(true)}>Open modal</button>

      <Modal isOpen={open} onClose={() => setOpen(false)} title="Hello!">
        <p>This is the modal content.</p>
        <button onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>Got it</button>
      </Modal>
    </>
  );
}
```

## Notes

- **Portal**: Rendering into `document.body` avoids z-index and overflow clipping problems from parent elements.
- **Backdrop click**: It uses `onMouseDown` rather than `onClick`, so dragging a text selection from inside the panel and releasing outside won't accidentally close it.
- **Focus**: The panel receives focus on open, and focus returns to the triggering element on close. For full focus trapping (Tab cycling inside the modal), consider adding a library like `focus-trap-react`.
- **Scroll lock**: Page scrolling is disabled while open and restored on close.

