## Notes

- **Backdrop:** `position: fixed; inset: 0` with a semi-transparent black fill covers the viewport. Flexbox centers the panel.
- **Click handling:** Clicking the backdrop closes the modal, and `stopPropagation` on the panel prevents clicks inside it from doing so.
- **Portal:** `createPortal` renders into `document.body`, which avoids z-index and overflow problems from parent elements.
- **Accessibility:** It uses `role="dialog"`, `aria-modal`, and focus management. For full focus trapping, consider adding a library like `focus-trap-react`.

# React Modal Component

This modal closes on Escape or a backdrop click, locks body scroll while open, and is accessible. It renders through a portal.

## `Modal.jsx`

```jsx
import { useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { createPortal } from "react-dom";
import "./Modal.css";

export default function Modal({ isOpen, onClose, title, children }) {
  const panelRef = useRef(null);
  const previouslyFocused = useRef(null);

  // Close on Escape
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;
    const onKeyDown = (e) => {
      if (e.key === "Escape") onClose();
    };
    document.addEventListener("keydown", onKeyDown);
    return () => document.removeEventListener("keydown", onKeyDown);
  }, [isOpen, onClose]);

  // Lock body scroll and manage focus
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isOpen) return;
    previouslyFocused.current = document.activeElement;
    const originalOverflow = document.body.style.overflow;
    document.body.style.overflow = "hidden";
    panelRef.current?.focus();

    return () => {
      document.body.style.overflow = originalOverflow;
      previouslyFocused.current?.focus?.();
    };
  }, [isOpen]);

  if (!isOpen) return null;

  return createPortal(
    <div className="modal-backdrop" onClick={onClose}>
      <div
        className="modal-panel"
        role="dialog"
        aria-modal="true"
        aria-labelledby={title ? "modal-title" : undefined}
        tabIndex={-1}
        ref={panelRef}
        onClick={(e) => e.stopPropagation()}
      >
        <button
          className="modal-close"
          onClick={onClose}
          aria-label="Close modal"
        >
          &times;
        </button>
        {title && (
          <h2 id="modal-title" className="modal-title">
            {title}
          </h2>
        )}
        <div className="modal-body">{children}</div>
      </div>
    </div>,
    document.body
  );
}
```

