- **`type="button"` by default** — a `<button>` inside a form defaults to `type="submit"`, which is a common source of accidental submits.
- **CSS custom properties** — override `--btn-bg`, `--btn-bg-hover`, etc. on a parent or via `className` to re-theme without touching the component.

### Extending it

If you need a loading state, add a `loading` prop and render a spinner alongside the label, then set `disabled={disabled || loading}` and `aria-busy={loading}`. Keep the label in the DOM (visually hidden if needed) so the button doesn't change width mid-interaction.

