# PrimaryButton Component

Here's a reusable React button component with hover and disabled states, written in TypeScript with Tailwind CSS:

```tsx
import React from 'react';

type PrimaryButtonProps = {
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onClick?: () => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
  type?: 'button' | 'submit' | 'reset';
  className?: string;
  'aria-label'?: string;
};

export const PrimaryButton: React.FC<PrimaryButtonProps> = ({
  children,
  onClick,
  disabled = false,
  type = 'button',
  className = '',
  'aria-label': ariaLabel,
}) => {
  return (
    <button
      type={type}
      onClick={onClick}
      disabled={disabled}
      aria-label={ariaLabel}
      className={[
        // Base styles
        'inline-flex items-center justify-center',
        'px-4 py-2 rounded-md',
        'text-sm font-medium text-white',
        'transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out',
        'focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-offset-2',
        'focus-visible:ring-blue-500',
        // Enabled state
        'bg-blue-600',
        // Hover state (only when not disabled)
        !disabled && 'hover:bg-blue-700 active:bg-blue-800',
        // Disabled state
        disabled && 'bg-blue-300 cursor-not-allowed opacity-60',
        className,
      ]
        .filter(Boolean)
        .join(' ')}
    >
      {children}
    </button>
  );
};
```

## Usage

```tsx
export default function App() {
  return (
    <div className="flex gap-3 p-6">
      <PrimaryButton onClick={() => alert('Clicked!')}>
        Save changes
      </PrimaryButton>

      <PrimaryButton disabled>
        Saving...
      </PrimaryButton>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Key design decisions

- **Hover only when enabled** — the `!disabled &&` guard prevents the hover styles from applying to a disabled button (which would otherwise show a misleading interactive cue).
- **`cursor-not-allowed`** — communicates that the button isn't clickable.
- **`opacity-60` + lighter background** — reduces visual weight so the disabled state is obvious at a glance.
- **`focus-visible` ring** — keyboard users get a clear focus indicator without the ring appearing on mouse clicks.
- **`aria-label` passthrough** — supports icon-only buttons or cases where the label text differs from the visible content.
- **`type` prop defaults to `"button"`** — prevents accidental form submissions when the button is placed inside a `<form>`.

