### Modal Behavior & Accessibility

This modal handles the details that make a dialog feel polished and accessible.

- **Backdrop dismissal** – Clicking the darkened backdrop closes the modal, but only when the press starts and ends on the backdrop itself, so dragging a text selection out of the panel won't dismiss it.
- **Keyboard support** – Pressing Escape closes the modal, and Tab cycles focus within the panel, keeping keyboard users inside the dialog.
- **Focus management** – When the modal opens, focus moves to the first focusable element inside the panel; when it closes, focus returns to the element that triggered it.
- **Scroll locking** – The page behind the modal is prevented from scrolling, with scrollbar width compensation to avoid layout shift.
- **Portal rendering** – The modal is rendered into `document.body` via `createPortal`, so it sits above all other content regardless of the parent stacking context.
---

**Optimization Tip:** You can adjust the backdrop color and blur in `.modal-backdrop`, and change the panel's `max-width` in `.modal-panel` to fit your design. The `title`, `footer`, and `ariaLabel` props let you customize the content and accessible name without touching the component internals.

